course: dictionary
lesson: 2443
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as numbers, and you pick the one that fits the sentence. «Never swim near dams or reservoirs; the water is cold and deep.» Reservoirs are lakes behind walls, so dam here means a strong wall built across a river.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «Beavers build dams that make ponds where many other animals live.» Beavers are animals, so this dam is the wall of sticks and mud a beaver builds across a stream.
explain: A word can also change its job. In «a dam», dam is a thing, so it is a noun. In «to dam a river», dam is an action, so it is a verb. Look at the small words around it, like "a" or "to", to see which job it is doing.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A dam is a strong wall built across a river or stream to hold back the water.
fact: The lake that forms behind a dam is called a reservoir.
fact: Beavers build dams from sticks and mud, and the water behind them makes ponds.
fact: As a verb, «to dam» means to build a dam across something, such as a river.
fact: A dam is also the mother of an animal, such as a horse or a dog.
exercise: «The dam holds back the water like the plug in a bath.» What does dam mean here? | A bridge for walking across | A fast current of water | *A wall built across a river to hold back water | A small pond full of mud
exercise: The workers will dam the river next spring. What does dam mean here? | To sing loudly | *To build a wall across a river | To dry up a pond | To swim fast in a river
exercise: In «to dam a river», what kind of word is dam? | *A verb, an action word | A full stop | An adjective, a describing word | A noun, a thing
test: What is a reservoir? | Ice that forms on a river in winter | *A lake that forms behind a dam | A type of beaver | A deep hole in the ground
test: A puppy's dam is | Its favourite toy | Its owner | *Its mother | Its bed
exam: «Alpine ibex climb the almost vertical walls of dams.» What does dam mean here? | A small goat with horns | A type of salt | A pond of mud | *A wall built across water to hold it back
